<title>USA: No end in sight to falling insurance rates - broke.</title>
<headline>No end in sight to falling insurance rates - broke.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>There is no end in sight to falling rates and low premium growth in the global insurance industry, according to a forecast by U.S insurance broker Johnson &amp; Higgins.</p>
<p>In a 162-page report released Tuesday, the broker predicted that insurance buyers could look forward to even lower prices, higher limits, and enhancements to coverage at little added cost in 1997.</p>
</text>
